---
import AltLayout from "../_alt/AltLayout.astro";
import { alternatives } from "../_alt/alternatives";
import Icon from "../_home/Icon.astro";
---

<AltLayout
  slug="index"
  title="Landing page alternatives"
  description="Six complete alternatives to the Archevolt landing page, built for review."
>
  <section class="alt-index" aria-labelledby="alt-index-title">
    <div class="frame">
      <p class="mono-label">Review build · not for publication</p>
      <h1 class="sec-title sec-title-wide" id="alt-index-title">Six ways to tell the same story</h1>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Every alternative keeps the current design and argues from the same three values: an ergonomic API,
        performance, and a flexible architecture. They differ in structure and copy. Each page is complete,
        and the review bar at the top moves between them.
      </p>
      <ol class="alt-index-list">
        {
          alternatives.map((alternative, index) => (
            <li>
              <a class="alt-index-card" href={`/alt/${alternative.slug}`}>
                <span class="mono-label">
                  {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")} · {alternative.origin}
                </span>
                <h2>{alternative.name}</h2>
                <p class="alt-index-shape">{alternative.shape}</p>
                <p>{alternative.summary}</p>
                <span class="pill">
                  Open
                  <Icon name="arrow-right" />
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <ul class="alt-index-notes">
        <li>
          Judge A's and judge B's structures refine the value spine and the question ladder. They are variations,
          not new shapes. "One argument" is the new shape, built from your note that the detail should come from
          the values.
        </li>
        <li>
          Numbers come from one machine. The SIMD kernel figures were measured on 5 November on main, and the kernel
          is not yet in a NuGet release.
        </li>
        <li>The <a href="/">current page</a> is unchanged. These pages are marked noindex.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</AltLayout>
